The validator recomputes every derived field and errors if impl_status, product_truth, the derived indexes, or any screen->mockup link has drifted from its source.

I/O boundary: After checking persisted artifacts, normal completion emits console diagnostics, a process exit code and a final stdout JSON outcome. --quiet changes logging verbosity only. Missing validation dependencies or a refused --tighten request return early before that outcome line.

The same validator verifies declared field paths, types, requiredness and defaults; complete and projected examples; observed receipt provenance; required metadata for every flow node; and drift in generated contract presentation. Declared proposed binding gaps remain visible and are counted separately from implemented interfaces.

